Phase OS-14: Kernel Security & Key Management Subsystem - 3 new AArch64 assembly kernel modules:

1. kernel/key_store.asm (Secure Key Storage)
   - Base ID: 904
   - Secure storage and management of cryptographic keys
   - Features: key generation (AES-128/192/256, RSA-2048/4096), key import/export (encrypted), key derivation (PBKDF2, HKDF), key wrapping/unwrapping, key rotation policies, access control, key usage tracking, secure deletion
   - Data structures: key_entry_t (id, type, size, flags, created, expires, usage_count, permissions, owner, wrapped_key[256], active), key_policy_t (rotation_days, max_usage, allowed_ops)
   - API: key_store_init, key_store_generate, key_store_import, key_store_export, key_store_derive, key_store_wrap, key_store_unwrap, key_store_delete, key_store_rotate
   - Capacity: 64 keys, 256 bytes per key, 8 key types
   - Pattern: follow kernel/crypto_aes.asm style (stp/ldp frame, .global exports, .bss for state)

2. kernel/pki_cert.asm (X.509 Certificate Management)
   - Base ID: 905
   - X.509 certificate validation and certificate chain management
   - Features: certificate parsing (DER/PEM), signature verification, certificate chain validation, CRL checking, OCSP client, certificate revocation tracking, trust store management, certificate expiration monitoring
   - Data structures: cert_t (id, version, serial, issuer, subject, not_before, not_after, pubkey, signature, chain_depth, revoked, trusted), trust_anchor_t (id, cert_id, constraints, active)
   - API: pki_cert_init, pki_cert_parse, pki_cert_verify, pki_cert_chain_validate, pki_cert_check_revocation, pki_cert_add_trust_anchor, pki_cert_revoke, pki_cert_check_expiry
   - Capacity: 32 certificates, 16 trust anchors, chain depth 8
   - Pattern: follow kernel/crypto_sha.asm style

3. kernel/audit_log.asm (Security Audit Logging)
   - Base ID: 906
   - Comprehensive security audit logging for compliance and forensics
   - Features: event logging (auth, file access, network, process), log levels (info, warning, error, critical), log rotation, log filtering by type/severity, log search/query, log integrity (HMAC), log export, real-time alerting hooks
   - Data structures: audit_event_t (id, timestamp, event_type, severity, pid, uid, resource, action, result, details[128]), audit_policy_t (event_mask, severity_filter, alert_threshold)
   - API: audit_log_init, audit_log_event, audit_log_query, audit_log_rotate, audit_log_set_policy, audit_log_integrity_check, audit_log_export, audit_log_alert
   - Capacity: 256 events in ring buffer, 16 event types, 4 severity levels
   - Pattern: follow kernel/net_tcp.asm style

Build all 3 kernel modules with:
  clang --target=aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu -c -O2 -o kernel/<name>.o kernel/<name>.asm

